ce-tips-dataset-1 = If you're on fire, you can click the alert on the right of your screen to stop, drop, and roll.
ce-tips-dataset-2 = You can view and edit all keybindings used in-game at any time through the Options menu.
ce-tips-dataset-3 = You can access the in-game guidebook through the escape menu, or by pressing Numpad 0 by default.
ce-tips-dataset-4 = Some entities ingame have guidebook entries associated with them, which you can view by examining the entity and clicking the question mark icon.
ce-tips-dataset-5 = Remember to touch grass in between playing Crystall Edge every once in a while.
ce-tips-dataset-6 = You can use the Activate in World keybind, E by default, to interact with objects while your hands are full, or without picking them up.
ce-tips-dataset-7 = Common sense goes a long way to avoiding conflict.
ce-tips-dataset-8 = Every other player in game is a human being as well.
ce-tips-dataset-9 = As a ghost, you can use the Verb Menu to orbit around and follow any entity in game automatically.
ce-tips-dataset-10 = Don't be afraid to ask for help, whether from your peers in character or through LOOC, or from admins!
ce-tips-dataset-11 = You'll quickly lose your interest in the game if you play to win and kill. If you find yourself doing this, take a step back and talk to people — it's a much better experience!
ce-tips-dataset-12 = If there's something you need from another department, try asking! This game isn't singleplayer and you'd be surprised what you can get accomplished together!
ce-tips-dataset-13 = We were all new once. Be patient and guide new players, especially those playing learning roles, in the right direction.
ce-tips-dataset-14 = Demoman takes skill.
ce-tips-dataset-15 = You can click on the names of items to pick them up in the right click menu, instead of hovering over the item and then selecting pick up.
ce-tips-dataset-16 = Crystall Edge is open source! If there's a change you want to make, or a simple item you want to add, then try contributing to the game. It's not as hard as you'd think it is.
ce-tips-dataset-17 = By right clicking on a player, and then clicking the heart icon, you can quickly examine them to check for injuries or how badly they're bleeding. You can also do this to yourself.
ce-tips-dataset-18 = Instead of picking it up, you can alt-click food to eat it. This also works for mice and other creatures without hands.
ce-tips-dataset-19 = If you want to stop your prisoner from escaping from the cell right after being uncuffed, turn on combat mode while uncuffing — this will shove the prisoner down.
ce-tips-dataset-20 = Bleeding is no joke! If you've been stabbed or acquired any other major injury, make sure to treat it quickly.
ce-tips-dataset-21 = Fire can spread to other players through touch! Be careful around flaming bodies or large crowds with people on fire in them.
ce-tips-dataset-22 = You can avoid slipping on most puddles by walking.
ce-tips-dataset-23 = Don't step on nails without shoes, they will hurt you. This also means if you are being chased by a carrin or carcat throwing nails behind you is a good way to escape.
ce-tips-dataset-24 = Always keep an emergency levitation amulet in one of your 2 belt slots, if you fall off the island it will prevent you from dying once.
ce-tips-dataset-25 = Each melee weapon has unique animations for both left click and right click, make sure to check them out!
ce-tips-dataset-26 = Be aware of what is blocking the lucson sphere from charging, you can see it by looking at a light monolith status projector. If it is on fire there is something happening.
ce-tips-dataset-27 = If you spot a pipe that is emitting blue light, dont go near it and get a technician to fix it.
ce-tips-dataset-28 = As a guard, make sure to keep your weapons charged, you can charge them by dropping them off on a charging platform and turning it on.
ce-tips-dataset-29 = As a guard, throw bolas found in the armory to slow down people you are pursuing.
ce-tips-dataset-30 = As a guard, the guardrail mace has 2 modes, the inactive mode allows you to hit people with it like any other weapon, the active mode allows you to shoot out orbs of mana that drain stamina.
ce-tips-dataset-31 = Everyone has a hidden role with their own objectives, be careful who you trust.
ce-tips-dataset-32 = As a professor, you can heat up a bottle with 2 types of essence to produce a new type, but make sure to check if the essence attractor nearby is turned on. Check the guidebook for recipes.
ce-tips-dataset-33 = As a professor, it is your job to deal with hungry nodes that pop up. First find it and examine what types of essences it needs. Then spill it nearby.
ce-tips-dataset-34 = As a student, make sure to grab thaumaturgy glasses and a thaumaturgic magnifying glass to be able to do your job.
ce-tips-dataset-35 = As a professor, you should find magical nodes that appear throughout the island. They offer essence and knowledge.
ce-tips-dataset-36 = If you are getting thirsty or hungry visit the tavern. It can also be a hotspot if you need help.
ce-tips-dataset-37 = As a chef, remember to add water to any soup recipe.
ce-tips-dataset-38 = As a chef, it is also your job to take care of the garden, plants need light and water to survive. Make sure to water them!
ce-tips-dataset-39 = As a chef, you can talk up the guests and gain some information if you listen well.
ce-tips-dataset-40 = To use a lockpick go up to a locked door and right click on it and select the keyhole option. Guess the combination a loud sound will play if you guess wrong. All doors with the same lock have the same combination.
ce-tips-dataset-41 = A mask can hide your identity just by putting it on. You may be suspicious though!
ce-tips-dataset-42 = Don't stay in the murk for too long unless you wish to join the shadows!
ce-tips-dataset-43 = In the bottom left of the screen there is an armor icon, that opens up your character menu with what your wearing, objectives, and skills. You can also open this with the U hotkey!
ce-tips-dataset-44 = As a werewolf, be careful when you transform. You are visible on the map for everyone to see however you block the charging of the lucson sphere.
ce-tips-dataset-45 = As a technician, make sure to grab your pickaxe and mining goggles so you can find ore nodes.
ce-tips-dataset-46 = As a technician, it is more efficient to set up automation on ore nodes you find. Set up a drill with a machine frame and a conveyor under it to transport the ore back to the furnaces.
ce-tips-dataset-47 = As a technician, you can change the recipes inside of furnaces to produce different materials you need. You can also put in any product from the furnaces again to transform it into a different one.
ce-tips-dataset-48 = As a technician, the energy scanner googles as well as the island power grid projector to find any broken pipes that may need repaired.
ce-tips-dataset-49 = As a technician, make sure you have the brass insulator armor on to prevent yourself from being fried by broken pipes.
ce-tips-dataset-50 = As someone who is jobless try and find something to do such as helping guards kill the nightmares that appear in the city.
ce-tips-dataset-51 = Tip #51 does not exist and has never existed. Ignore any rumors to the contrary.
ce-tips-dataset-52 = Meow?
ce-tips-dataset-53 = If a werewolf screams at you and you are shaking. Run away as fast as you can and scream for help. You can not fight back.
